this, a self governing group of boys. They have some

237
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:46,130
things to go by, but they get to govern themselves. They get to make their

238
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:49,890
own decisions. And this is. Do you remember being this age?

239
00:16:50,130 --> 00:16:53,330
If you go back and you think about this age, if you think about yourself

240
00:16:53,830 --> 00:16:56,850
at this age, one of the things you really were looking for was some freedom.

241
00:16:57,650 --> 00:17:00,530
You wanted the definition and the support of your family.

242
00:17:01,810 --> 00:17:05,160
You wanted the definition and support of society,

243
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:08,720
but you also wanted to be free. You also wanted

244
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:13,080
to have some self determination. And this is, you know, it's a natural part of

245
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:17,520
developing as a person. And so you start testing boundaries and

246
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:21,200
you start seeing just how far you can get with things. And if people really

247
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:24,920
mean what they say and all those things that happen during adolescence,

248
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:29,320
well, being a part of Scouting and being a part of a patrol that

249
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:31,400
has real freehanded responsibility,

250
00:17:33,060 --> 00:17:36,740
that is going to be an important thing to

251
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:40,380
the development of your personality and the way

252
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:44,020
that you're going to begin to interact with the rest of the world. Back to

253
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:48,620
AIDS of Scoutmastership and Baden Powell talks about the values

254
00:17:49,120 --> 00:17:53,140
of the patrol system. It's important that the Scoutmaster recognize the extraordinary

255
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:57,940
value which he can get out of the patrol system. It is the best guarantee

256
00:17:58,440 --> 00:18:02,320
for permanent vitality and success for the troop. It takes

257
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:06,680
a great deal of minor routine work off the shoulders of the Scoutmaster. But first

258
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:10,840
and foremost, the patrol is the character school for the individual.

259
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:15,680
To the patrol leader it gives practice and responsibility and in

260
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:20,360
the qualities of leadership. To the Scout it gives subordination

261
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:24,440
of self to the interests of the whole. The elements of self denial and

262
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:28,600
self control involved in the team spirit of cooperation and good comradeship.

263
00:18:29,710 --> 00:18:33,870
But to get first class results from this system, you have to give the boyleaders

264
00:18:34,190 --> 00:18:38,030
real free handed responsibility. If you only give partial

265
00:18:38,530 --> 00:18:42,590
responsibility, you only get partial results. The main object

266
00:18:43,150 --> 00:18:46,510
is not so much in saving the Scoutmaster trouble as to give

267
00:18:47,010 --> 00:18:50,830
responsibility to the boy. Since this is the very best of all

268
00:18:51,330 --> 00:18:54,990
means for developing character. The Scoutmaster who hopes for success

269
00:18:55,070 --> 00:18:58,330
must not only study what is written about the patrol system

270
00:18:58,830 --> 00:19:02,610
and its methods, but must put into practice the suggestions that he reads.

271
00:19:03,110 --> 00:19:06,370
It is the doing of things that is so important.

272
00:19:08,290 --> 00:19:12,610
It is the doing of things that is so important. And only by constant

273
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:17,090
trial can experience be gained by the patrol leader and his

274
00:19:17,590 --> 00:19:20,370
Scouts. The more he gives them to do,

275
00:19:20,850 --> 00:19:24,710
the more they will respond, the more strength and character they will achieve.

276
00:19:25,350 --> 00:19:29,350
So this central innovation, this most important

277
00:19:29,510 --> 00:19:32,950
part of Scouting, is one thing for us to

278
00:19:33,450 --> 00:19:37,230
really focus on and to concentrate on as leaders. And as I've said many,

279
00:19:37,730 --> 00:19:42,030
many times, this is not a program so

280
00:19:42,530 --> 00:19:45,990
much as a process. This is not a way

281
00:19:46,230 --> 00:19:49,330
of efficiently managing a group of boys.

282
00:19:50,050 --> 00:19:53,410
This is a process that they go through, this patrol system.

283
00:19:53,650 --> 00:19:57,290
And it's something that our founder reminds us, hey, we have

284
00:19:57,790 --> 00:20:01,170
to study it, we have to understand it, we have to constantly work

285
00:20:01,670 --> 00:20:04,610
with it, and that it is never arriving.

286
00:20:05,570 --> 00:20:09,090
It's a constant journey. So that's the great innovation.

287
00:20:09,570 --> 00:20:13,210
That is the one essential feature in which Scouting differs

288
00:20:13,710 --> 00:20:17,290
from everything else, and here's why. A lot of times we're missing

289
00:20:17,790 --> 00:20:20,970
the boat on the patrol system because it's so simple.

290
00:20:21,450 --> 00:20:25,090
A lot of times we're missing the boat on the implementing and

291
00:20:25,590 --> 00:20:29,330
applying the patrol method, the patrol system, to Scouting because it

292
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:33,450
is really just that simple. We'd like it to be a little more complex.

293
00:20:34,410 --> 00:20:37,810
It does have a lot of complexity, but it's complex in

294
00:20:38,310 --> 00:20:41,540
the same way that driving a golf ball or hammering a nail

295
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:45,100
or going up to bat in baseball is

296
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:48,780
complex. I mean, anybody can take a

