00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:52,900
bat, a hammer, a driver in their hand,

298
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:56,820
and hit a nail or a baseball or a golf ball.

299
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:59,940
Right? Anybody can pretty much manage that.

300
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:04,340
But how many books have been written and movies have been shot?

301
00:21:04,420 --> 00:21:08,140
And how much advice has

302
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:12,370
there been about how to get a perfect drive or how

303
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:16,730
to hit a baseball out of the stadium or how to drive a nail properly?

304
00:21:16,890 --> 00:21:20,170
I mean, these things are deceptively easy to

305
00:21:20,670 --> 00:21:22,570
look at. They're easy for somebody to try,

306
00:21:23,610 --> 00:21:26,810
but getting really good at it, I mean, that's what takes a lot of

307
00:21:27,310 --> 00:21:30,930
concentration, a lot of thought, and a lot of analysis.

308
00:21:31,430 --> 00:21:35,090
And that's what we're constantly up to here. That's what we're constantly

309
00:21:35,590 --> 00:21:39,280
up to, is analyzing this, thinking about it, looking at it, and in

